                <pb facs="0468" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.30/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-10T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 10,
                                1919—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your October 27, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to inform the <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Government
                    that the question of permitting a naval commission to go to Peru, is receiving
                    the Department’s serious consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
